        { q:'On a memory-constrained device with no O(n) extra space, what\'s the next-best Two Sum approach?', options:['Brute force O(n²) is unavoidable','Sort + two-pointer: O(n log n) time, O(1) extra space','Use bit manipulation'], answerIdx:1, explanation:'Sort + converging two-pointer beats brute force on time and matches the space constraint. (You\'d need an index map if positions matter.)' },
        { q:'If the array could be VERY large but you only need the first valid pair, does Two Sum support early termination?', options:['Yes — return on first hit, never need to finish the array','No, you must scan the whole array','Only with sorted input'], answerIdx:0, explanation:'<code>return</code> bails out at the first pair found. If the answer is near the start, you never visit the rest.' }
