        { q:'For "kSum" generalized, the recursive structure is:', options:['Sort + recurse: kSum(target) = for each i, (k−1)Sum(target − nums[i]) on nums[i+1..]','Brute force only','Cannot be generalized'], answerIdx:0, explanation:'Pick an anchor; recurse to find (k-1)-Sum on the rest. Base case is 2-Sum (two-pointer). Total O(n^(k−1)). Same duplicate-skipping logic at each level.' },
        { q:'After finding a valid triplet in 3Sum, you also skip duplicates inside the inner loop. What\'s the rule?', options:['Skip nothing','While L &lt; R AND nums[L] == nums[L+1]: L++; same for R from the right','Skip after the loop'], answerIdx:1, explanation:'Once you record a triplet, duplicate values at L or R would re-emit the same triplet. Advance L past all equal-to-current values; same for R. THEN advance once more to leave the matched pair.' }
